### Register a tool with custom shell rendering

Source: https://github.com/earendil-works/pi/blob/main/packages/coding-agent/docs/extensions.md

Define a tool that manages its own shell by setting renderShell to 'self' and implementing renderCall.

```typescript
pi.registerTool({
  name: "my_tool",
  label: "My Tool",
  description: "Custom shell example",
  parameters: Type.Object({}),
  renderShell: "self",
  async execute() {
    return { content: [{ type: "text", text: "ok" }], details: undefined };
  },
  renderCall(args, theme, context) {
    return new Text(theme.fg("accent", "my custom shell"), 0, 0);
  },
});
```

--------------------------------

### renderResult(result, options, theme, context)

Source: https://github.com/earendil-works/pi/blob/main/packages/coding-agent/docs/extensions.md

Renders the tool result or output. Supports streaming via isPartial and detail-on-demand via expanded.

```APIDOC
## renderResult(result, options, theme, context)

### Description
Customizes the rendering of the tool result. Returns a Component instance.

### Parameters
- **result** (object) - The output returned by the tool execution.
- **options** (object) - Includes expanded (boolean) and isPartial (boolean) flags.
- **theme** (object) - The active theme for styling.
- **context** (object) - Contains state, lastComponent, and metadata.
```

--------------------------------

### renderCall(args, theme, context)

Source: https://github.com/earendil-works/pi/blob/main/packages/coding-agent/docs/extensions.md

Renders the tool call or header component. Receives arguments, theme, and a context object containing state and control methods.

```APIDOC
## renderCall(args, theme, context)

### Description
Customizes the rendering of the tool call header. Returns a Component instance.

### Parameters
- **args** (object) - The current tool call arguments.
- **theme** (object) - The active theme for styling.
- **context** (object) - Contains state, lastComponent, invalidate(), and metadata like toolCallId, cwd, isPartial, etc.
```

--------------------------------

### Register a custom tool with pi.registerTool

Source: https://github.com/earendil-works/pi/blob/main/packages/coding-agent/docs/extensions.md

Defines a custom tool with schema validation, execution logic, and optional custom rendering. Use promptSnippet and promptGuidelines to integrate the tool into the LLM's available context.

```typescript
import { Type } from "typebox";
import { StringEnum } from "@earendil-works/pi-ai";

pi.registerTool({
  name: "my_tool",
  label: "My Tool",
  description: "What this tool does",
  promptSnippet: "Summarize or transform text according to action",
  promptGuidelines: ["Use my_tool when the user asks to summarize previously generated text."],
  parameters: Type.Object({
    action: StringEnum(["list", "add"] as const),
    text: Type.Optional(Type.String()),
  }),
  prepareArguments(args) {
    // Optional compatibility shim. Runs before schema validation.
    // Return the current schema shape, for example to fold legacy fields
    // into the modern parameter object.
    return args;
  },

  async execute(toolCallId, params, signal, onUpdate, ctx) {
    // Stream progress
    onUpdate?.({ content: [{ type: "text", text: "Working..." }] });

    return {
      content: [{ type: "text", text: "Done" }],
      details: { result: "..." },
    };
  },

  // Optional: Custom rendering
  renderCall(args, theme, context) { ... },
  renderResult(result, options, theme, context) { ... },
});
```

### Custom Rendering

Source: https://github.com/earendil-works/pi/blob/main/packages/coding-agent/docs/extensions.md

Tools can implement custom TUI displays using renderCall and renderResult. By default, tool output is wrapped in a Box component, but setting renderShell to 'self' allows a tool to manage its own framing, padding, and background. If a slot renderer is not defined, the system uses a fallback rendering mechanism.

